      "created_at": "2024-11-07T12:26:46Z",
      "updated_at": "2024-11-07T12:26:46Z",
      "body": "There's an issue with the 3.11 backport, in `textiowrapper_change_encoding`. Main had:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n+    Py_INCREF(errors);\r\n ...\r\n     Py_SETREF(self->encoding, encoding);\r\n-    Py_SETREF(self->errors, Py_NewRef(errors));\r\n+    Py_SETREF(self->errors, errors);\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut in 3.11 this is:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n+    Py_INCREF(errors);\r\n...\r\n     Py_INCREF(errors);\r\n     Py_SETREF(self->encoding, encoding);\r\n     Py_SETREF(self->errors, errors);\r\n```\r\ni.e. there's an extra incref, but it looks -- at least to Git -- like the change that removes `Py_NewRef` was already applied.\r\n\r\nThis was not caught because [`test_io` *refleaks* tests were ineffective on 3.11](https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/126478#issuecomment-2462070264).\r\n\r\nI'm preparing a fix.",
